Dear Area Chair,

We would like to briefly summarize the discussion that took place during the rebuttal period. Reviewers raised concerns regarding:
- Hallucination issues in our hierarchically generated caption dataset and the effectiveness of disentangled representation learning;
- Whether recent VLMs exhibit bag-of-words-like behavior, revealing limitations in current disentanglement approaches;
- The value of additional evaluations on open-vocabulary detection benchmarks.

We addressed these concerns thoroughly in our response. Reviewers **PuqX** and **19CP** commented that their initial concerns were reasonably clarified and recommended the paper for acceptance. Although we did not receive follow-up comments from **z1ZV** and **MTQ7**, their concerns aligned with previously discussed points, and we believe they were addressed in the same context.

To support our response, we conducted additional experiments, including:
- Expanded evaluation of the HiVG dataset and LLM-based recaption datasets (Qwen3, GPT);
- Embedding analysis of recent VLMs (Qwen-VL, E5-V) and failure-case studies;
- Evaluation of OOD generalization on OmniLabel and D³, with additional results on ODinW and gRefCOCO.

All corresponding improvements have been added into the revised manuscript.
Thank you very much for taking the time to review our work.
